      "sequence_position": 15,
      "problem": "If $p=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $q=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$, then $p\\cdot q=$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}+{p}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}+{p}_{3}\\cdot {q}_{3}+{p}_{4}\\cdot {q}_{4}+{p}_{5}\\cdot {q}_{5} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-3)+(-2)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-10-4-4-9-10 \\\\  & =-37\\end{aligned}\n$$",
